_url":"https://github.com/peterbell10","id":13238737,"login":"peterbell10","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjM4NzM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peterbell10","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> Is this behavior expected (output buffer reuse between candidate runs)?\n\nYes this is expected behavior. The autotuner just calls your kernel with the provided arguments multiple times to run the benchmarks. It's up to the user to ensure that these configs are well tested and produce the same solution. \n\n> Should Triton warn/error when autotuned kernels can leave parts of outputs unwritten unless reset_to_zero / restore_value is specified?\n\nThe autotuner doesn't really know what tensors are even outputs, so this wouldn't be very practical. Perhaps this could be added as an additional debug mode check, but nobody on our side is looking into this.\n\n> This possible to add this restore_value here:\n\nThat kernel doesn't initialize the accumulator from C, so shouldn't need `restore_value`.","created_at":"2026-02-02T17:22:49Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/9230#issuecomment-3836614387","id":3836614387,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/9230","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs7krhbz","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/3836614387/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-02-02T17:22:49Z","url"